\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A1}{\ignorespaces  Univariate transfer-active predictive distribution for river flow on the $\qopname  \relax o{log}(1+x)$ scale, with $x$ measured in m$^3$/s, at the December 25, 2022 forecast origin. Observed measurements before the origin are shown in green, and held-out USGS verification after the origin is shown in red. The pink ribbon is the pointwise central 95\% predictive interval (2.5th--97.5th percentiles), and the dark line is the predictive mean on the \(\qopname  \relax o{log}(1+x)\) scale. The ten thin traces connect synthesized predictive sample values. The origin line marks \(T\), and the first forecast lead is \(T+1\). The reference uses the USGS observation channel and transfer covariates, and excludes the external source channels. Horizontal guides use the same discharge references as Figure\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:synth1}. \relax }}{21}{figure.caption.26}}
